# Docs metadata: README tables, SECURITY table and the "At a glance" box are generated from
# this (dev/gen-docs.py). One "key: value" per line.
emoji: 🔐
name: Shared KDE wallet
group: core
what: One wallet for desktop mode *and* VR, an unlock dialog that works on the desktop, 4-hour auto-lock, a **Lock Wallet** button, closing that really locks, password-gated apps, and CLI credentials (`gh`) kept out of plain-text files.
why: The Frame runs two sessions (VR and a nested desktop) with separate D-Bus buses, so apps get two wallets that overwrite each other. The VR-side password prompt floats in VR, and terminal tools find no keyring at all. SteamOS's stock wallet has no password.
changes: `wallet-unlock`, `wallet-launcher`, `wallet-gate`, user service `wallet-lock-sync`, `kwalletrc` setting; rewrites chosen apps' menu entries (originals kept in `~/.local/share/frame-tweaks/launcher-originals`)
access: Talks to KDE Wallet over D-Bus; **closes KDE's own wallet password prompts** (replaced by its dialog); moves the GitHub CLI token into the wallet
survives-updates: Yes (everything is in your home folder)
undo: `./install.sh uninstall wallet` (keeps the wallet itself and KWalletManager; restores the KDE settings it changed)
